      "role": "user",
      "content": "i checked the mounts and piping, everything is rock solid. it's just that the chatter has this almost... mischievous quality to it? like it's purposely waiting for me to finish the job and then it starts up again just to mess with me. it's so unpredictable and weirdly rhythmic, almost like a little creature is tapping on the inside of the housing. is there any actual mechanical phenomenon where something can move or vibrate in a way that seems purposefully erratic or \"sneaky\" like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
